# =============================================================================
# Secrets
# =============================================================================
# The root .env configures the docker compose stack and holds the MySQL
# passwords, the JWT secret and the PayU salt. Never commit it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# TLS material for the Nginx container.
docker/nginx/certs/*
!docker/nginx/certs/.gitkeep

# =============================================================================
# Internal documentation
# =============================================================================
# docs/SECURITY-REVIEW.md contains exploit-level detail that should not live in
# the repository; see the README's security section for the summary instead.
#
# Note this is `docs/*` and not `docs/` - git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is itself excluded, and decisions.md must stay tracked.
docs/*

# The superseded exploit-level review, removed from HEAD in package 3.0 (U-5,
# SEC-17's open half). A copy is kept at docs/for_ocean_security_review.md,
# which docs/* already excludes. This rule exists so that a future `git add -A`
# from the repository root cannot quietly put it back.
for_ocean_security_review.md

# Architectural decision records ARE tracked: they explain why the schema and
# topology look the way they do, and a future contributor needs them.
!docs/decisions.md

# The remediation map IS tracked, because SPEC-3 section 5 requires every
# package to update it in the same commit as the work - a gate that cannot be
# enforced on an untracked file.
#
# THIS IS A DELIBERATE TRADE-OFF, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. The map names OPEN
# vulnerabilities with file and line (SEC-06 at payment.js:601, SEC-07 at
# payment.js:99, and so on), which on a public repository is a prioritised list
# of what is not yet fixed.
#
# PHASE 6 GATE: publication requires EITHER zero open findings in the map, OR
# the map redacted of file and line for everything still open.
#
# Note what the gate is not. A map of CLOSED findings with file and line is
# fine to publish and is good practice - it is evidence that the findings were
# fixed. The exposure exists only while items are open.
!docs/remediation-map.md

# The entity ownership audit IS tracked, for the same reason and with the same
# trade-off. AR1 made it a per-package gate: it must be re-run at the end of
# every package that moves an entity, and a gate cannot be enforced on an
# untracked file. The map references it, and a tracked document pointing at an
# untracked one is a dangling reference of exactly the kind this project keeps
# finding.
#
# IT CARRIES THE SAME EXPOSURE. It names open findings with file and line -
# payment.js:141 as the donation writer, admin.js:234 as the password writer -
# which is a map of where the seams are. THE PHASE 6 PUBLICATION GATE COVERS
# THIS FILE TOO: zero open findings, or redacted of file and line.
!docs/entity-ownership-audit.md

# =============================================================================
# Node
# =============================================================================
node_modules/
